subject: test(models): regression test for fetch timeout guard (GAP-P2-18)

The AbortController + 5s timeout on fetchCompatibleModelIds() already exists
at HEAD (upstream commit 838d9a7a, 2026-04-10) — the gap scanner flagged a
false positive because it searched for AbortSignal.timeout() while the code
uses the equivalent AbortController pattern.

This regression test locks the behavior so the guard cannot be silently
removed:

- fetch is called with the provider URL and a signal (AbortSignal)
- buildModelsList returns [] in bounded time when upstream hangs
- signal reaches fetch and is aborted (anti-false-positive assertion)

Anti-false-positive verified: intentionally removing the signal wiring from
route.js makes both tests time out and fail; restoring returns to 2/2 pass.

